      "writtenOn": "2024-06-14T18:56:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is basically the same for all the backends. Setting aside the complexities of directly writing spir-v, we could just have this write the `floatBufferArrayField.owner()` and then construct the field access and index expression manually in each language with a hard-coded set of appends to avoid having to re-create IR.\n\nThat said, creating the FieldAccess and VariableReference are pretty lightweight if we\u0027re coming from a memory pool. Do we have to clone the index expression node `c.arguments()[0]`? Or can we just reference it in `floatBufferArrayIndex`?\n\nIf we can avoid that clone, maybe instead of having a per-backend hard-coded handling of the expression (as I initially proposed), we just take this IR construction logic and move it to a shared function for the backend generators to call? @Arman do you know if such a place exists for universal polyfills?",
